 i had said to stephen that sounds  great count me in  i'm on board and then immediately called  my father and  asked him what stephen had been talking  about the riots in chicago  i had a vague sense that there had been  some civil unrest  uh at the democratic convention you've  said that directing chicago seven was  one of the most challenging things  you've ever done  yes it was incredibly challenging though  i  i had a lot of help from the cast of  course and a great team of designers but  first of all writing is challenging for  me uh writing a screenplay  directing is new to me you talk about  how challenging  writing can be for you i've read that  you can be very animated when you're  writing  yeah um  if anybody saw me writing they would  they would have been locked up i'm  very physical i'm talking out loud i'm  playing all the parts  uh i'm i'm jumping up and down uh uh  from my desk  uh i've without really realizing i was  doing it i've i've  walked like blocks away from my office  um uh while i was talking to myself  uh but those those are the great moments  those are like when you've  when you've got it uh and it's working  those are the really great moments the  bad moments  are are when you're frozen in front of a  blank screen with a flashing cursor one  of the most powerful  uh moments in the film is when  uh bobby seal ends up in in shackles  basically  in the courtroom that's not an  exaggeration is it  no uh first of all nothing in the film  is an exaggeration  all of this happened but surely  uh the the most terrible moment of the  trial  uh is when as you said bobby seal is  taken away  roughed up by some u.s marshals uh  shackled  a gag put in his mouth sort of tape  around  the guy he was bound and gagged in an  american courtroom  you recently reunited with the original  cast of the west wing  to benefit michelle obama's voter  turnout initiative what was it like  collaborating with them again  that was fantastic it is a benefit for  when we